1
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:58,500
Lyle Swann is a champion off-road racer. But to the people of
1877, he's something very, very different...

2
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Timerider: The Adventure of Lyle Swann is a science
fiction, western film directed by William Dear.

3
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:43,500
Lyle Swann is a successful off-road racer who
mistakenly gets sent back in time 100 years.

4
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:36,000
When a band of outlaws robs Swann of his motorcycle, he's forced to outfox the
gangsters and give in to the seductions of a gorgeous local lady.

5
00:29:22,500 --> 00:29:28,500
With only his smarts and a map from an Exxon station, Lyle must try to make it
out of the Old West alive and find a way back to modern times.

6
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:21,000
Lyle Swann, played by Fred Ward.

7
00:41:07,500 --> 00:41:13,500
Porter Reese, played by Peter Coyote.

8
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Ben Potter, played by L.Q. Jones.

9
00:52:52,500 --> 00:52:58,500
Carl Dorsett, played by Tracey Walter.

10
00:58:45,000 --> 00:58:51,000
Claude Dorsett, played by Richard Masur.

11
01:04:37,500 --> 01:04:43,500
Claire Cygne, played by Belinda Bauer.

12
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
Timerider: The Adventure of Lyle Swann is a 1982 American science fiction Western film directed by William Dear and starring
Fred Ward as Lyle Swann, a cross country dirt bike racer in the 1980s who is mistakenly sent back in time to 1877.

13
01:16:22,500 --> 01:16:28,500
The film was scored, produced and co-written (with
director William Dear) by Michael Nesmith.

14
01:22:15,000 --> 01:22:21,000
The film explores themes of mexico, experiment, time travel, revenge, shootout.

15
01:28:07,500 --> 01:28:13,500
The tone is thought_provoking.
